# NEGATIVE, BOTH-LANE (RV-A self-host mirror): `.field` on a String — a
# primitive receiver has no named fields. Rust gg rejects with E_NoFieldFound;
# the self-host typechecker mirrors it via infer.gg's RTPrimitive arm
# (DkNoFieldFound → E_NoFieldFound), closing the lane divergence where the
# self-host silently ACCEPTED `s.data` and lowered an int64-0 placeholder.
int main():
    String s = "hello"
    print(s.data)
    return 0
